.TH SSH-TO 1 "September 2026" "Version 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ssh-to \- symlink-driven transparent SSH shortcut manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssh-to
[\fBlink\fR|\fBunlink\fR|\fBlist\fR|\fBsync\fR|\fBpath\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B <host>
[\fISSH-OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ssh-to
eliminates repetitive \fBssh\fR invocations by dynamically determining the target
hostname from \fB$0\fR (the invoking symlink basename). It manages an isolated directory
of host symlinks and allows transparent execution directly from the shell prompt.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BI link \ host...
Create one or more host shortcut symlinks pointing to \fBssh-to\fR.
.TP
.BI unlink \ host...
Remove host shortcuts.
.TP
.B list
List all configured host shortcuts.
.TP
.B sync
Scan \fI~/.ssh/config\fR for Host entries and automatically generate shortcuts.
.TP
.B path
Print the machines directory path intended for \fB$PATH\fR inclusion.
.SH EXAMPLES
Register servers manually:
.IP
.nf
ssh-to link dev-server prod-bastion
prod-bastion -p 2222
.fi
.PP
Automatically sync all hosts defined in your SSH config:
.IP
.nf
ssh-to sync
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Crafted for sovereign POSIX environments.
